    "turn_text": "This episode of Against the Grain is brought to you by The Hotline. National Journal now offers a free hotline newsletters for non-members that covers all the most important political news of the day with concise summaries and linked sources for further reading. You can subscribe at go.nationaljournal.com slash subscribe dash hotline. Live from my home office. Welcome to the Socially Distanced Against the Grain Podcast. I'm Josh Krausar, Politics Editor of National Journal, and I'm very pleased to be joined today by former Republican Congressman Denver Riggleman from the great state of Virginia, my own home state here. Riggleman served in the house between 2018 to 2020 in Virginia's fifth district around Charlottesville. And he was ousted by right wing activists at a subsequent Republican convention in 2020. Riggleman is a former U.S. Air Force intelligence officer and currently CEO of Riggleman Information and Intelligence Group. He is also the co-owner of the award-winning Silverback Distillery and he's also the author of one of the more intriguing titled books in political history. Bigfoot, it's an",
