  {
    "episode_id": 49226,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49226.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "I think you have some strong policy people. I mean friends of mine that I still was shocked that voted to not accept the electors to this day. I still understand why they did it for political reasons. And like I said, I know we're already coming full circle only a little bit into this podcast. But the issue that we had is that they had to get reelected and they would say, well Denver, I might have to say things that are a little crazy to beat the crazier's, right? That's the rationale. For me, I just, Josh, I did not have the ability to do it. It's almost like I had a tick. Like anytime somebody said you had to do something, I don't actually push to get it. Now that could push against it. Now that could be my family might say, including my wife and daughters, even as a military officer, my problem with authority, right? I do not like to be dictated to. And I certainly don't want to be dictated to the people that I think, you know, maybe have been sniffing glue too long that night, right? And, you know, and that's, that's the issue is that I had a really difficult time doing that, but you had to sort of There was no way to get around having some kind of implicit support from Donald Trump to get through any type of election, the Republican Party in 2018. And it was funny, even when he endorsed me for the run, his endorsement was a little weaker there, but he else and people laughed about it. And it was because I just don't think he wanted to endorse me. And I'm okay with that. And we haven't had a discussion with our consultants. I said, do we accept this? And I'm like, well, you have to. And that's just some of the things that you dealt with. And it just got worse and worse for me as I went through this. And to the point that I got pretty, as you know, pretty outspoken about disinformation, QAnon, and the fact that we needed a party that was policy over sort of the cold of personality that you see right now. So there's strong policy people to answer the question in a longer way. But again, loyalty first, policy second, that's really what it comes down to in the GOP.",
