    "turn_idx": 32,
    "turn_text": "So you're seeing people that are spouting, unadulterated bullshit, pulling in piles of cash. The grift is working. And so when you look at that and you look at the polling again and you're seeing that You know, say Liz Cheney is upside down on Wyoming, or you see Fred Upton's upside down in Michigan, or you see the Tom Rice's upside down in South Carolina, you see that Anthony Gonzalez is upside down in Ohio, and I'm not sure if they see this. But what I'm saying is that polling and fundraising determine the message from the Republican leader. And I'm not making a judgment of morality one way or the other. I've been in the conference. That's what dictates where you're going is your messaging and your polling. And then how you pull that off and the purge of Liz came down to the fact that she wanted to talk about facts and integrity, not messaging and polling specifically on things that were obviously untrue and, and I applaud her for that I think that's what you need in leadership is you need that ability. to cut through sort of the morass of polling and fundraising crazy in order to speak truth. And I really admire her for that. And I like to say that there's a lot more like that, but I think the group is very small. I count myself as one of them, but I think it's a very small group.",
