  {
    "episode_id": 49226,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49226.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 35,
    "turn_text": "Josh, if you're a conservative, you've got to fight a two-flank war. I don't know. I think there is a threat to democracy for disinformation, and I think there's a threat of radicalization and violence, as you know, that's my background. I think that is extremely important. I think what you're seeing from the Democrats, though, and I think why I sort of a head scratcher to me that they also have a unique ability to pull failure out of the jaws of success, right? And I find it interesting that some of the policies are talking about like six trillion in funding. You see the inflation rate going up. that they're talking about raising taxes after a dismal time for everybody going through COVID because I own companies and how awful it was to try to keep employees. I just find it interesting that they're going so far left that it's making it difficult for Republicans who want to come into them and to the middle to work with them even if they think that Trump should be absolutely just annihilated from the Republican Party. So again, yes, democracy number one is the thing we should absolutely protect. But it would be interesting. I would be saying these same things like Liz's if I was still elected, but I'd also be saying there's no way that I'm voting for some of these bills. They're horrendous, right? And the name of the bills don't match the language. And you see so much ridiculousness on the floor like the past few days with what's going on in Israel right now in Palestine and with Hamas. And it's just amazing to me. that the Democrats should see what true, I would say, fringe ideological politics can do to a party and yet they still want to go there now. I think it's making it very difficult for Republicans, even like me or even like the Antonese or the John Cat Coast, to actually reach across the aisle because some of the stuff is just not in line with what conservative values are.",
