  {
    "episode_id": 49226,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49226.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, the threat is significant. And the reason is, is because we see this in the data. I'm also the chief strategist for the Network Contagion Research Institute. And what we're seeing is that Trump was sort of the, I would say was the nexus of QAnon, right? He was sort of the messianic or apocalyptic figure that people followed, and then it was sort of Q being the intermediary to pass that information based on coded language or memes. right, or Q drops and things of that nature. I think though what we've seen in data is you've seen it switch from QAnon back to New World Order is that Trump might have been the focus or the nexus, you know, the what people were contouring on with QAnon, but he also identified the enemy. And the enemy is the deep state cabal, it's COVID-19, it's vaccinations, even though with it's so interesting to watch anti-vaxxers rise up within the QAnon New World Order, portion of this based on Operation Warp Speed and stuff like that. But he's identified the enemy. And now the focal point isn't Trump anymore. It's the deep state or trying to control people based on those conspiracy theories. So what we've started here is a disinformation virus. And I think it's metastasized based on the number of social media network channels that people can access. And again, that's what we're trying to fight is how do we stop pre-selection of echo chambers An individual almost main lighting these main lining these electrons into their frontal lobes. It's very difficult to stop, but I think it's actually getting a little bit worse when it comes to how people are privately sort of hoarding these type of ideas and these type of conspiracy theories.",
