    "turn_idx": 44,
    "turn_text": "That's fantastic. Somebody asked me that today. I don't know if there's anything specifically comparable to QAnon, right? When I don't know if there's Democrats accusing Republicans of accosting children and creating a drain of chrome from their blood during their heightened sense of fear on metal station or killing, right? I don't know if that's a thing. I do think though that when you look at the fringe left, they automatically jump to racism, fascism, and you want to call it wokeness. It isn't even that. It's almost an ignorant look. uh, at groups as a whole. The one thing that I've, I've worn people about is you don't want to dehumanize people as a group. And when I hear the left say this, well, you can't be a Republican and believe in democracy. Well, that's poppycock, right? That's, that's you trying to dehumanize an entire group based on your own worldview. And that's exactly how dehumanization or how violence happens. Right now again, I'm just giving that as an example. I'm not saying that the left, you know, has this massive, you know, charter to destroy all Republicans because they think that there are some kind of Mar-a-Lago bootleckers. I'm not saying that. What I am saying, though, is that it can metastasize. And what we're seeing right now, and things that are going to get crazy for us, as you know, again, I'm in the NCRI, we put out the QAnon reports, we put out the N.A. Semitism and white supremacy reports. We're having a report coming out on how BLM, some people who say their BLM are using coded language to organize violence. And that is going to make people on the left their heads explode, right? Or Antifa, because if you look at the facts and the data, it puts you in a very strong position to identify the ideological gaslighting that goes on based on people who want to make money. And Josh, that's where I'm going here. It's all about file the money. It's all about the grift. So if something's crazy and it's making money and you know it's crazy, it is about the grifters that are pushing that, pushing that message. And we have to be very aware of that on the right and the left. But as far as the left having something completely identical to the QAnon stuff, I don't see it yet, but it doesn't mean that they won't mirror image or there won't be a reaction to that. But we're certainly seeing the far left using coded language and memes to organize violence. And that is incredibly dangerous also.",
