    "turn_idx": 46,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I can't imagine me jumping right into a tribe specifically. And I'm just going to say this, and I have a lot of Democrat friends. I'll never be a Democrat. And, you know, but it's almost like what I ever be a Republican again, either, like is a self-described, you know, chest-thumping Republican, probably not either. I feel like the one kid in the Lord of the Flies that got away and started something new right on the beach. But that's, you know, I'm sort of willingly tribalized right now, but I do believe, I think there's really, you know, I've seen people say, you know, the Republican Party is beyond repair or it can't be saved. I reject that. That's, again, you know, you're trying to, and there's friends of mine who say that, right? I mean, people I respect and I'll have whiskey with every time like Denver you just need to leave the Republican Party like official like get on air and say I'm done with it and I've come close Josh I'll be honest with you I've come close I think about doing it every day. The thing is though is I'm waiting a little bit because that's what Intel guys do is they look at the data and the analysis we're still a long way from 2022. even though I believe that the messaging is already baked in when it comes to stop the steel election integrity and Trump loyalty will be, you know, the things that Republicans will run on in 22. I think we have a real chance maybe to bring back sort of this practical conservatism. It's the best way I can say it. It's not compassion, it's just practical, rational conservatism that knows that, you know, an out of control government, a large government can really destroy our way of life, right, and what we built as United States citizens. And I really sort of love that feeling of being that guy, but I'm also more social libertarian. So I think maybe a third movement might come at some point. I think it's needed. I think the two-party system are just two corporations that are trying to really fleece people, and they just get as crazy as they can during the primary season, and then they try to, you know, I would say in a very awkward way, get back to the middle. So I don't know what I am. I would say that I'm an American. I think that's really what it comes down to. That leans right. That wishes I could say Republicans refer the things I believe in right now. But I've said this and you've heard this before. I did not leave the Republican Party. The Republican Party left me. And it certainly left me that day on the floor when I was the only one talking against QAnon. And everybody looked at me like I had a weird growth coming out of the middle of my forehead. That's really what it came down to.",
