    "turn_text": "Well, I think, you know, I always find it funny, you know, Terry coming back, but I think he's just trying to get ready, you know, Virginia is just a sort of a stepping stone for him for further office, right, Josh? I mean, anybody who doesn't see that is, you know, I think maybe drunk on their own bathwater. But I think I think when you're talking about Glenn, I had some high hopes for Glenn. I still think he's the best they could have done in the awful convention they had, but only 29,000 people out of 5.8 million registered voters participated. That's absolutely egregious. That's anti-American. However, I'll say this is that he did have to run into the election integrity stop the steel way to even do this or to have a chance to win. I think he's going to have a difficult time getting over the Trump endorsement and some of the things that he said, some of the ads that he ran, but Glenn is no dummy. And I think when you look at what he's accomplished, he had a real chance to really change the dynamic, I think of the Republican Party, but he realized and his consultants told him that the polling did not allow him to do that. He had to run very far right on social issues and he had to run sort of into the, I would say the Mar-a-Lago camp of issue screaming, which was really, you know, election integrity commissions and stuff like that. But I think you underestimate Glenn at your own peril. He's well-funded. He can fund himself. He's very good on the stump. I think I'm damn good on the stump and it's hard to impress me and Glenn's very good. So I think people better be careful if they think this is some kind of walkover for Terry. based on his background or if Terry's going to win or if the progressive portion of the Virginia Democrats lose their mind, this could be really interesting. And again, that means that you could have somebody who ran on sort of a stop the steel background for a very limited convention to win the general because the left is not doing the right thing post-COVID. And again, that's why it's a head scratcher to me is why do you go full crazy when you barely have a mandate, right? Josh, it's just, and that's why we need that third party. I know I'm coming back to your original question. We need this third movement to balance out the fringes on the left and the right for sure.",
