    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/9/49226.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 54,
    "turn_text": "I don't know. It's going to come down to the business model that they're presenting, but my biggest worry is tax increases and again, trying to manipulate the economy based on things that might or might not be true. I think that's very dangerous. But it's hard for me. If I could take away stop the steel election integrity and all that nonsense, I would lean towards Glenn. Obviously and but again, I'm also not specifically and Josh's could be news I'm not the most religious guy, but I'm probably the one who wants to protect religious liberty the most So since I have that I'm sort of a science-based guy I'm probably not as strong on life issues as people would want me to be as a Republican either, you know if I believe in you know health of the mother and rape and incest exceptions and And also believe in science that, you know, up to 20 weeks, it should be probably a decision between, you know, the mother, the father and their health care provider. After 20 weeks, there should be more restrictions based on science. I'm sort of out of step with the right and the left, right, Josh, I'm again, I'm tribalist. So it puts me in an interesting position as being somebody who's very independent minded. who wants people to have as much freedom as possible, who despises government overreach and bullies, but I also despise corporate overreach. So I don't know what I am. I'm sort of like this bizarre, you know, American have some libertarian values, some social democratic values, some Republican fiscal values. So it puts me in a really bizarre sort of situation, but I'll be damned if I'm gonna vote for somebody who says stop the steal or the election was stolen. I won't do that. So it would put me in a pretty awkward position because I don't know if Terry's message is right for Virginia either.",
