    "turn_idx": 56,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think a lot of moderate Republicans will vote for Terry. There's no doubt about it, but I don't even know if that's moderate anymore. I mean, what is a squish? I think a squish of somebody who shows their belly to Donald Trump because they crawl over broken glass to get his blessing, right? That's a squish. You know, somebody with absolutely no moral compass and right. And somebody who would rather win than anything else. You know, I think of squishes, you know, like, you know, people running for governor that, you know, have to go down to Trump and have dinner with him and Probably have to pour his damn coffee. So I think really what you have is you're going to have this sort of courageous center with a backbone that's going to have to get aggressive. You're going to have to be intellectually confrontational. And I think that is the voter, right? And somebody says, listen, I am done, you know, with some gas bag, you know, rolling out things that aren't true. And I'm done with sort of this government overreach, like, you know, bureaucrats that have been in the political system somehow know how to run a business or can't make a decision on whether you wear a mask or not. You know, that's, and that's, I am that voter, right? I am that guy, right? I hate government and aptitude. And I despise a party that follows one person. And that, my God, I mean, maybe, maybe I should move to Greenland, you know? I don't know. I don't know, Josh. It's, I think I am that voter. And I think there's a lot of us out",
