    "turn_text": "First of all, I don't think the Democrats have realized yet that the economy is still a pretty big damn issue, right? The other thing I don't think Democrats have realized is how engaged Trump supporters are specifically, and the Republican Party is rallying behind that because they feel they're being unduly ostracized, demonized, dehumanized, actually putting in a bucket that everybody's the same. And what happens is if you're in one tribe, even if you think there's crazy people in the tribe, like, hey, Johnny over there likes to cover himself in feces, but it's better than those guys over there, right Josh? The issue is, are you choosing between crazy and crazier? And I think a lot of Democrats are becoming disengaged, especially on the moderate side, because you do see sort of this screaming that's going on about certain social issues or certain foreign policy issues, I would say even more than social issues.",
